{"step_index":32,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T11:44:15Z","content":"Good — `video_watch` costs 25 credits (not 10 as I thought earlier) and runs async. Now firing both tools simultaneously with research-informed prompts:","tool_calls":[{"name":"call_mcp_tool","args":{"Arguments":{"prompt":"You are analyzing this video's EDITING AND ANIMATION PRODUCTION STYLE for a creator who wants to replicate this format as a faceless 2D animated history channel. Produce a detailed Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) covering EVERY editing technique visible in this video. Be extremely specific and technical:\n\n1. ANIMATION STYLE: What type of 2D animation is used? Are these custom illustrated characters or template-based? How are they animated (frame-by-frame, puppet rigging, simple transforms)? What level of detail do characters have?\n\n2. TEXT ANIMATIONS: Every instance of on-screen text — what font style, what motion type (pop-in, slide, typewriter, kinetic typography?), placement (center, lower-third, full-screen?), duration on screen, color/outline treatment. Note EACH different text style used.\n\n3. TRANSITIONS: Document every transition type between scenes. Hard cuts, animated wipes, map pans, camera zooms? What percentage are hard cuts vs animated transitions?\n\n4. CAMERA WORK IN 2D: How do they simulate camera movement within flat art? Zooms, pans, tracking shots, parallax layers? How fast are these moves? What easing curves?\n\n5. COLOR & VISUAL TREATMENT: Color palette (specific hex ranges if visible), contrast level, any filters/LUTs applied, background treatment, lighting simulation in 2D.\n\n6. MAPS & DIAGRAMS: How are maps styled? How do territory changes animate? How are timelines presented? What overlays are used for geopolitical explanations?\n\n7. PACING & CUT RHYTHM: Average shot duration, how many cuts per minute, where do holds happen, where do rapid-fire sequences happen? Time-stamp specific examples.\n\n8. SOUND DESIGN: SFX usage frequency and types (whooshes, impacts, comedic hits, ambient), music bed changes, how audio transitions between segments, narrator pacing sync with visual edits.\n\n9. RECURRING VISUAL PATTERNS: Any repeated visual motifs, intro/outro style, thumbnail style connections to video content, recurring graphic elements.\n\n10. PRODUCIBILITY SOP: Step-by-step workflow a SOLO creator would follow to produce one video in this style. Include specific software recommendations, asset creation pipeline, editing sequence, and realistic time estimates per step.\n\nFormat as a structured SOP document with clear sections and specific technical details. Do NOT be vague — I need exact techniques, not descriptions like 'they use nice animations'.","video":"https://youtu.be/fXuWQg7uJKg"},"ServerName":"vidiq","ToolName":"vidiq_video_watch","toolAction":"Analyzing video editing style","toolSummary":"VidIQ video watch"}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$env:PYTHONIOENCODING='utf-8'; Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_watch.json\" -Value '{\"videoUrl\": \"https://youtu.be/fXuWQg7uJKg\", \"question\": \"You are analyzing this video EDITING AND ANIMATION PRODUCTION STYLE for a creator who wants to replicate this format as a faceless 2D animated history channel. Produce a detailed Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) covering EVERY editing technique visible in this video. Be extremely specific and technical: 1. ANIMATION STYLE: What type of 2D animation is used? Custom illustrated characters or template-based? How are they animated (frame-by-frame, puppet rigging, simple transforms)? Detail level of characters? 2. TEXT ANIMATIONS: Every on-screen text instance - font style, motion type (pop-in, slide, typewriter, kinetic typography?), placement (center, lower-third, full-screen?), duration, color/outline treatment. Note each different text style. 3. TRANSITIONS: Document every transition type. Hard cuts, animated wipes, map pans, camera zooms? What