\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TEXT & TYPOGRAPHY\\n\\n*   **Primary Font:** Heavy, rounded, bold comic/display sans-serif (e.g., *Komika Axis*, *Obelix Pro*, or *BadaBoom BB*).\\n*   **Color Treatment:** \\n    *   *Standard:* Pure White fill with a heavy 8–12px black solid stroke and a soft drop shadow (offset down-right).\\n    *   *Accents/Dynasties:* Muted gold/yellow or crimson fills matching historical flags/factions.\\n*   **Motion Types:**\\n    *   **Pop-in / Punch Scale:** Scale from 0% to 115% over 4 frames, easing back down to 100% over 3 frames with an accompanying hit SFX.\\n    *   **Stamp/Slam:** Scale down rapidly from 250% to 100% with immediate camera shake upon landing.\\n    *   **Wiggle/Float:** Continuous subtle rotation oscillation (±2–3°) for comedic or lingering captions.\\n*   **Placement & Duration:** Center-screen for title/chapter cards; lower-third or pinned directly above specific territory shapes/characters for 1.5 to 3.5 seconds.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. TRANSITIONS & SCENE CUTS\\n\\n*   **Hard Cuts (75% of video):** Direct cuts timed precisely to voiceover sentence clauses and comedic punchlines.\\n*   **Dynamic Zooms / Snap Zooms (15%):** Instant 1–2 frame scale-ins into a character's shocked face or an expanding map region.\\n*   **Map Pans / Slides (5%):** Smooth directional slides (left-to-right, north-to-south) across painted territory backgrounds.\\n*   **Thematic Graphic Wipes (5%):** Ink splatters, torn paper peeling, rolling scrolls, or sliding wooden signs clearing the frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. 2D CAMERA SYSTEM\\n\\n*   **Simulated 2D Moves:** Layered camera rigs in 2D space to establish depth between foreground characters, midground elements, and map/scenery backgrounds.\\n*   **Easing Curves:** Aggressive Bezier easing (Fast Out / Slow In or Exponential Deceleration). Quick snaps (8–12 frames) followed by static or slow-drift holds.\\n*   **Parallax Effect:** 3-layer parallax setup on landscape scenes (Foreground foliage moving at 100% speed, Midground characters at 60%, Background mountains/sky at 20%).\\n*   **Camera Shake:** High-frequency, decaying 4–6 frame positional jitter applied during explosions, weapon impacts, and dynasty collapse animations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. COLOR PALETTE & VISUAL ASSETS\\n\\n*   **Palette:**\\n    *   *Map Grounds:* Desaturated parchment, warm beige (`#E8D8B8`), light olive/tan paper tones.\\n    *   *Faction Identifiers:* Solid, distinct, medium-saturation hues (Han = Cyan/Teal, Qin = Terracotta Orange, Jin = Crimson/Red, Song = Deep Violet/Purple, Yuan = Solid Pitch Black).\\n*   **Shading:** Cel-shading style. Flat base colors with single-layer hard-edged multiply shadows (30% opacity black/deep purple) along lower curves.\\n*   **Textures:** Subtle paper/canvas overlay on top of all visual layers set to *Overlay* or *Multiply* mode at 5–10% opacity to eliminate flat digital sterility.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. MAPS & TERRITORY ANIMATIONS\\n\\n*   **Map Base:** Hand-drawn stylized regional contours with thick outer boundary lines and clean interior borders.\\n*   **Territory Transitions:**\\n    *   *Expansion:* Fluid shape-layer path morphing or solid color flood fills expanding outward from capital nodes.\\n    *   *Fragmentation:* Fractured glass line overlays appearing over 2 frames, followed by instant split-color shifts for newly broken warlord states.\\n*   **Date/Timeline HUD:** Persistent, standardized rectangular timeline box placed in the bottom-right corner (Parchment fill, black border, bold monospace/sans numbers) updating with rapid rolling-number keyframes on era transitions.\\n*   **Faction Mini-Icons:** Floating circular or shape badges in the top-left corner displaying the active ruling house.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. PACING & EDITING RHYTHM\\n\\n*   **Average Shot Duration:** 1.5 to 2.8 seconds per visual beat.\\n*   **Cuts Per Minute:** ~25 to 35 cuts/scene changes per minute.\\n*   **Pacing Structure:**\\n    *   *Narrative Beats (Holds):* 3 to 4-second dialogue holds for core character interactions, visual jokes, or dialogue exchanges.\\n    *   *Montage/War Sequences:* Rapid-fire 0.5 to 1.2-second bursts of maps fracturing, marching icons, and sliding weapons during multi-state warfare segments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. SOUND DESIGN & AUDIO SYNC\\n\\n*   **Narration Alignment:** Visual actions lead narration by 1–2 frames; punchlines cut simultaneously on the exact consonant peak of the voiceover.\\n*   **SFX Density:** 1 SFX every 1.5–2 seconds.\\n    *   *UI/Motion:* Whooshes, pops, wooden clacks, page turns, rubber stretch sounds for character poses.\\n    *   *Action/Warfare:* Cartoon sword slashes, muffled explosions, comedic thuds, laser beams, glass shattering.\\n*   **Music Selection & Ducking:** Lighthearted, bouncy, upbeat orchestral or retro-gaming acoustic tracks. Aggressive sidechain ducking (-14dB to -18dB) beneath voiceover, surging during non-verbal slapstick moments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. RECURRING VISUAL PATTERNS & MOTIFS\\n\\n*   **The \\\"Warring States\\\" Wooden Sign:** Hanging wooden plank graphic dropping from the top border on a spring hinge, flipping a counter upward each time the region fractures into civil war.\\n*   **Personified Maps:** Countries/territory blobs animated with eyes and mouth shapes directly on the landmass to express fear, anger, smugness, or defeat.\\n*   **Pop-Culture Visual Parodies:** Sudden stylistic shifts parodying video games (Pokémon evolution screens, 8-bit platformers), retro news broadcasts, or comic book panels.\\n*   **Imperial Headdresses:** Exaggerated, dangling beaded scholar hats acting as the primary symbol of sovereign authority.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. SOLO CREATOR WORKFLOW & PIPELINE\\n\\n### Software Toolkit\\n*   **Illustration/Asset Creation:** Adobe Illustrator / Clip Studio Paint / Inkscape.\\n*   **Animation & Motion Design:** Adobe After Effects / Moho Pro.\\n*   **Audio Editing & Mastering:** Audacity / Adobe Audition.\\n*   **Video Assembly & Final Grade:** Adobe Premiere Pro / DaVinci Resolve.\\n\\n### Production Pipeline & Time Estimates (per 10-Minute Finished Video)\\n\\n| Phase | Tasks & Deliverables | Est. Solo Time |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **1. Script & VO** | Research history, write comedic narrative, record VO, edit audio track with breath removal and EQ/compression. | 8 – 12 hrs |\\n| **2. Asset Prep** | Illustrate base maps, modular puppet parts, generic peasant/soldier rigs, UI cards, and icon sets in vector format. | 15 – 20 hrs |\\n| **3. Layout & Animatic** | Place VO in timeline; generate rough blocking, timed still images, and camera positions. | 6 – 8 hrs |\\n| **4. Motion & Rigging** | Keyframe character puppets, map territory morphs, text pop-ins, and secondary motion. | 25 – 35 hrs |\\n| **5. SFX & Polish** | Layer sound effects, dynamic music tracks, screen shakes, paper textures, and render out master file. | 8 – 10 hrs |\\n| **TOTAL** | Complete cycle for a high-retention 10-minute explainer. | **62 – 85 hrs** |\"},\"refunded\":false,\"message\":null,\"_credits\":{\"used\":0}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
